    "pw.signInAgain": "Leave the Hub",
    "w.check.databases": "the list of this device's databases",
    "w.check.caches": "the list of this device's caches",
    "faq.lockProtects.a": "The passcode lock is part of the Hub on the web; the Hub in a terminal has none. On the web, once locked, people who pick up your device see only the lock screen. It locks after the time you pick, and when you leave the app if you turn that on; inside a Board program it can wait up to 15 minutes longer. Each tab and window locks and unlocks on its own; Lock now locks them all. It doesn't encrypt your sign-in: someone who can read what the web Hub stores on the device (developer tools, malware, a rooted phone) can still use it. The phone may show a preview of the Hub in its app switcher. Your account on other devices is not affected.",
    "faq.lockScope.q": "Where does the passcode apply, and what removes it?",
    "faq.lockScope.a": "The lock belongs to the Hub on the web, in the one place you set it; the Hub in a terminal has none. There, each tab and window locks on its own, and opening the Hub again asks for the passcode. Signing out keeps the passcode there; to remove it, use Remove passcode, or the Forget action on its lock screen. After you sign in again, the Hub still asks for it. Clearing the site's data removes the lock and signs you out of the Hub there. Notices already shown on that device stay there.",
    "pw.unsureTitle": "Leave the Hub and sign in again",
    "check.unknownPw": "We cannot tell from here whether the password was changed. It may have been. Leave the Hub, then sign in again with the new password; if that fails, the old one still works.",
    "check.checkLinePw": "Check again: reads your account again, but it can't show whether the password changed. Signing in after you leave the Hub shows which password works.",
    "faq.checkAgain.a": "When the Hub can't tell whether a change went through, it keeps a note instead of calling it done or failed. Check again reads your account again to see whether the change is there; if it still can't tell, the note stays. Stop tracking makes the Hub stop following the change. It doesn't undo the change or mark it as failed, and doing the change again may apply it twice. For a password change, signing in after you leave the Hub shows which password works."
