    "faq.scope.a": "Global entries are shared by every realm and by tools that run without one. The entries of a realm belong to that realm. The same name in another realm, or in Global, is a different entry. Pick a realm from the realm menu at the top (Alt+R) to see its own entries.",
    "faq.showValue.a": "Open the entry and press Show value to show it, or Copy to copy it without showing it. The value is read only then. Hiding it or closing the entry removes it from this page; the next press reads it again. An encrypted value asks for its password first; the password never leaves this device. JSON values are shown formatted, with Raw for the exact text; Copy always copies the exact stored value. You can also show the encrypted form, to paste where a tool expects it.",
    "faq.encrypt.a": 'The value is encrypted on this device before it is sent, and tools need the password to read it. To open an encrypted value here, enter its password; the password never leaves this device. An entry shown as "Not marked" has no encryption recorded. To protect its value, use Replace value and tick Encrypt with a password. The Hoody SDK, CLI and agent use the same encrypted form, so they can read it with the password.',
